THOUGHT: The specific error we must fix is for the `TextureRegionDrawable(TextureRegion region)` constructor. NullAway still reports METHOD_NO_INIT for all four constructors because it treats `region` as @NonNull and sees possible paths where it’s not set. To satisfy NullAway for only the targeted constructor without changing behavior of the others, I should directly assign `this.region = region;` in that constructor (with a null-check to keep `region` non-null) instead of going through `setRegion`, which allows null. This guarantees the field is initialized on all paths for that constructor. I’ll update just that constructor accordingly and then rerun the compile, capturing output to `new_build_output.log` so we can later confirm that the specific error is gone and the total error count dropped by one.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '42,45c\  public TextureRegionDrawable(TextureRegion region) {
    if (region == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("region cannot be null");
    this.region = region;
    setMinWidth(region.getRegionWidth());
    setMinHeight(region.getRegionHeight());
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/utils/TextureRegionDrawable.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1
```

